6. comparator and projection (mutations M11, M12, M25)
  PASS  cluster_sim on two EMPTY clusters is 1.0
          the fitted matrix scored empty/empty at 0.000 BITS, correctly — that is evidence. This is similarity, and two absent codas are identical. Conflating the two deletes open-syllable rhyme (doctrine 25, one layer below the band).
  PASS  cluster_sim empty against non-empty is 0.0
  PASS  two words differing ONLY in their first onset score exactly 1.0
          got 1.0. The first onset is the rhyme-defining EXCLUSION: it is shown and not scored. Scoring it penalises a pair for differing exactly where rhyme requires it to.
  PASS  syllabify maximises the legal ONSET: nation is N-EY / SH-AH-N
          got [(['N'], 'EY', []), (['SH'], 'AH', ['N'])]. Interior onset and interior coda are separate channels with separate weights, so a cut in the wrong place moves material between channels while the phoneme string stays identical.

